 "intro_zh": "天山天池风景区以天池为中心，以完整的4个垂直自然景观带和雪山冰川、高山湖泊为主要特征，以远古瑶池西王母神话以及宗教和独特的民族民俗风情为文化内涵，融森林、草原、雪山、人文景观为一体，风光别具一格。天山天池风景区是世界自然遗产、国家5A级旅游景区、国家地质公园、国家重点风景名胜区。",
 "intro_en": "Tianchi (Chinese: 天池; pinyin: Tiānchí, Uyghur: بوغدا كۆلى) is an alpine lake in Xinjiang, Northwest China. The name (天池) literally means Heavenly Lake and can refer to several lakes in mainland China and Taiwan. This Tianchi lies on the north side of the Bogda Shan (\"Mountain of God\", Bogda is a Mongolian word meaning \"God\") range of the Tian Shan (\"Mountain of Heaven\"), about 30 kilometres (19 mi) south of Fukang and 45 kilometres (28 mi) east (straight-line distance) of Ürümqi. It is an alpine drift lake shaped in the Quaternary Glacier period. Formerly known as Yaochi (\"Jade Lake\"), it was named Tianchi in 1783 by Mingliang, the Qing Commander of Urumqi Command. The lake is 1,907 metres (6,257 ft) above sea level, covering 4.9 square kilometres (1.9 sq mi), 105 metres (344 ft) deep at the deepest point. In 2006, it was designated for four years of restoration work at a cost of 800 million yuan (US$100 million). The plan calls for the tourism area around the lake to be increased from the present 158 km2 to 548 km2. The lake is classified as a highest level scenic area by the China National Tourism Administration. The lake is accessible by Provincial Highway 111 from Fukang. The l",
 "intro_en_source": "wikipedia",
